# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# KCD, 82 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with capture through Windows.Graphics.Capture (-wgc), the mouse pointer in the picture and the frames that change less than a tenth of the largest area changed in the last half second left out, the frame pool on a device of its own and its textures opened on the present's device, 2026-10-21, build e2c8058; cut to the stretch the stream's video shows, 52.4 s to 5005.4 s
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description KCD, 82 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with capture through Windows.Graphics.Capture (-wgc), the mouse pointer in the picture and the frames that change less than a tenth of the largest area changed in the last half second left out, the frame pool on a device of its own and its textures opened on the present's device, 2026-10-21, build e2c8058; cut to the stretch the stream's video shows, 52.4 s to 5005.4 s
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 42
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 0.9
field_pull_wraps 81
#
# WHAT IT COVERS: the 2026-10-21 stream, 82 minutes cut to the gameplay its video shows,
# captured through Windows.Graphics.Capture with the mouse pointer in the picture, the frames
# that change less than a tenth of the largest area changed in the last half second left out
# before the ring (28393 of them over the whole log), and the frame pool on a device of its own
# whose textures the present opens through shared handles. The policy is the one the tree ships.
# The game hitched (20 to 100 ms) 398 times an hour and stalled for 100 ms or more 102 times an
# hour, the most of any stream here, in 131 bursts, 89 of them with a stall, and with no periodic
# stretch. The lock released 14 times (10 an hour): 7 of them 0.2 to 1.4 s after a burst of
# hitches (at 395.6, 672.9, 1320.4, 1321.0, 1685.4, 1849.7 and 4354.8 s), and 7 with no hitch of
# 20 ms or more in the 3 s before (at 2021.9, 2528.2, 2534.2, 2534.5, 2534.8, 2676.1 and 2727.1
# s), four of those within 6.6 s. The worst blend run, 42 presents from 4354.7 s, is the last
# release, 0.25 s after two hitches of up to 41 ms. Of the 68 moves on the replay, 21 land more
# than 2 ms from a real frame.
#
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 52.431 s, from the 2272
# marked frames in its first 38 s, 2131 of them on time and within 0.40 ms of that offset (p90).
# The video runs 4953.0 s with no holes, opens on gameplay and ends on gameplay after a cutscene,
# so the cut is the whole video, 52.4 s to 5005.4 s of log time, and the marked frames lie inside
# it. Every second inside the cut that falls out of the 60 fps regime is a hitch second, 54 of
# them in 52 runs, none longer than 2 s, so nothing was removed from the middle.
#
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay reads synth 0.9% against 0.9%, worst run 39 against 42 (42 on the dejitter arm, which is
# how the stream ran), runs >= 50 0 against 0 and pull wraps 78 against 81. Counted over this
# window on the dejitter arm, blends are 2781 against 2799, repeats 1681 against 1676, skips 347
# against 347, and lock releases 14 against 14, each at the same moment. The replay makes 68
# moves, 11 of them late, and the field's log has 66 in the window. The 18 blends, 5 repeats, 3
# pull wraps and 2 moves by which the two differ were not traced present by present. With each
# wake's flush time added (2026-10-28), the replay's pull wraps are 80 against the field's 81,
# and the pull-wrap bound is measured there.
#
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran. The worst run's bound is the
# dejitter arm's 42, not the plain replay's 39, since both arms are held to it.
max_worst_run 42
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 1.3
min_reseeds 147
max_pull_wraps 80
extra_lag_ms 75
